---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
---

<!-- Orphan page: reached by direct link only. Not linked from Nav/Footer, noindex,
     and excluded from the sitemap (see astro.config.mjs). -->
<BaseLayout
  title="Resources | humAIn"
  description="Resources from humAIn 2026 speakers and partners."
  noindex
>
  <Nav />
  <main>
    <PageHeader secNum="— Resources" title="Resources" lede="Thank you for attending humAIn 2026. Here are the resources shared by our speakers." />
    <div class="res-page">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="res-body rv">

          <figure class="res-fig">
            <img src="/images/resources/stage-what-remains-human.jpg" width="1400" height="786" alt="A speaker on stage at humAIn beside a large screen reading “What remains human. Human remains.”" loading="lazy" />
          </figure>

          <section>
            <p class="res-thanks">Thanks to our content partner R/GA</p>
            <h2>Can brands think for themselves</h2>
            <figure class="res-fig res-fig--sq">
              <img src="/images/resources/rga-session.jpg" width="1400" height="1400" alt="Two speakers on stage at humAIn beneath the title “Can brands think for themselves?”" loading="lazy" />
            </figure>
            <p>Thanks for coming along to humAIn. AI now sits between brands and their customers, and most brands are using it for scale. Our Global CEO Robin Forbes and APAC Executive Strategy Director Marie Conley opened the conference by asking whether brands can think for themselves. Not on their own. The ones that stay distinct are the ones where people decide what the brand stands for first, then built that into the system.</p>
            <p>If you’d like to keep talking, I’d love to hear from you at <a href="mailto:victoria.curro@rga.com">victoria.curro@rga.com</a>.</p>
          </section>

          <section>
            <h2>Unstereotype Alliance: the Who’s Missing?</h2>
            <figure class="res-fig">
              <img src="/images/resources/unstereotype-panel.jpg" width="1400" height="932" alt="A panel of four speakers seated on stage beside a slide showing a QR code for the 3Cs Playbook for Inclusive AI" loading="lazy" />
            </figure>
            <p>Unstereotype Alliance Australia, convened by UN Women, is calling on the advertising, media and marketing industry to embed inclusive thinking from the start of every campaign by asking one powerful question: Who’s Missing? Backed by research linking inclusion to stronger brand outcomes, the <a href="https://www.unstereotypealliance.org/en/resources/research-and-tools/whos-missing-toolkit">Who’s Missing? toolkit</a> offers practical prompts and resources to help teams challenge assumptions, widen the frame and consider whose voices, experiences and perspectives are missing.</p>
            <p>The Who’s Missing? AI guidance extends this mindset to generative AI, encouraging us to ask ourselves better questions and make critical thinking a habit across research, briefing, creation, review and approval.</p>
            <p>Alongside it, the Unstereotype Alliance’s <a href="https://www.unstereotypealliance.org/en/resources/research-and-tools/the-3cs-playbook-skills-for-an-inclusive-ai-approach">3Cs Playbook: Skills for Inclusive AI</a> builds three core skills - Curate, Craft and Control - to help marketers recognise bias, challenge stereotypical defaults and strengthen human oversight when using AI.</p>
            <p>Together, these resources help teams create more inclusive, relevant and commercially powerful work.</p>
            <p>We are open to new members interested in creating inclusive, unstereotyped work and contributing to collective industry change. To learn more about the guidance or joining the Alliance, please email Annie at <a href="mailto:anna.konieczny@unwomen.org">anna.konieczny@unwomen.org</a></p>
          </section>

          <section>
            <h2>Gust PR</h2>
            <figure class="res-fig res-fig--sq">
              <img src="/images/resources/gust-pr.jpg" width="1400" height="1400" alt="A speaker presenting at humAIn in front of a screen of article cards" loading="lazy" />
            </figure>
            <p>AI Upfront startup Gust PR is looking to hear from nimble marketing teams who want more predictability and visibility into their PR.</p>
            <p>Founder Marie Dowling said the insights, expertise and conversations shared at HumAIn Media showed how important bespoke solutions are for AI transformation and adoption across marketing, media and creative teams. This is why Gust PR is looking to interview marketing and comms leaders to understand how they currently measure, report and improve earned media performance, exploring a new "Build Your Own" product that could easily plug into existing systems.</p>
            <p>Marie is also offering a complimentary media-verse audit to any brand that wants to see where it stands against its competitors.</p>
            <p>If you're interested or for more information, contact <a href="mailto:marie@newsary.co">Marie</a>.</p>
          </section>

          <section>
            <h2>The cost of being overlooked</h2>
            <figure class="res-fig">
              <img src="/images/resources/leoprd-session.jpg" width="1400" height="933" alt="A speaker presenting to an audience beside a slide titled Reputation to Revenue" loading="lazy" />
            </figure>
            <p>Following her session at HumAIn, <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/celiaharding/">Celia Harding</a>, Founder of <a href="https://leoprd.io/">LEOPRD</a>, shares new research into how AI is changing the way people make decisions and how brands can influence the answers and recommendations they receive.</p>
            <p>Drawing on over 420,000 real-world AI prompts and 200,000 AI responses, Reputation to Revenue 2026 reveals what people are really asking AI, why some brands get recommended while others are overlooked, and what this means for the future of marketing and communications.</p>
            <p>Download the report <a href="https://report.leoprd.io/">here</a>.</p>
          </section>

          <section>
            <h2>OI: original intelligence offer</h2>
            <figure class="res-fig">
              <img src="/images/resources/screen-swap.jpg" width="1400" height="1050" alt="A hand-printed humAIn banner with hearts, light bulbs, robots and grass" loading="lazy" />
            </figure>
            <p>As a humAIn 2026 delegate, book a Screen Swap team session before 30 November and receive a complimentary collective banner activation*, a handprinted keepsake your whole team contributes to on the day, and yours to display.</p>
            <p>Quote the code HUMAIN26 upon enquiry: <a href="https://thescreenery.com.au/pages/screen-swap-enquiry">https://thescreenery.com.au/pages/screen-swap-enquiry</a></p>
            <p>*Banner framing available as an optional add on. Offer ends Nov 30th 2026.</p>
            <p>Visit - <a href="https://thescreenery.com.au/pages/screenswap">https://thescreenery.com.au/pages/screenswap</a></p>
            <p>Attached <a href="https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Zr-qXldr2ImkgNztI3cEZ1rqmmdovhPT/view?usp=drive_link">flyer</a> and <a href="https://drive.google.com/file/d/1uSJjsllTAI1FRr64hioO1JXuTZUYJPFi/view?usp=drive_link">presentation</a></p>
          </section>

          <section>
            <h2>Your brand is invisible to AI.</h2>
            <figure class="res-fig res-fig--tall">
              <img src="/images/resources/obsessd.jpg" width="1050" height="1400" alt="Two people standing either side of a pull-up banner reading “Your brand is invisible to AI. We fix that.”" loading="lazy" />
            </figure>
            <p>HumAIn made the case that the AI conversation is better with people in it: candid, independent, playful and sometimes leftfield. The big question is – how do we codify this humanness to ensure the output, or ‘Brand DNA’ is preserved? Obsessd is an Australian AI discoverability consultancy that helps brands take control of this space. We co-design full funnel prompts, audit what large language models (LLM) say about a brand, score it on the Obsessd Visibility Index ™ (OVI), then fix the content and code that AI retrieves. In our latest research we found some of Australia’s leading CPG and Pet Care brands were invisible to AI for use case, occasion or need-based prompts. Name the product and AI finds you. Describe the need and it doesn’t.</p>
            <p>Read the findings and what to do about them: <a href="https://obsessd.ai/blog/name-the-product">https://obsessd.ai/blog/name-the-product</a> More information: <a href="mailto:hello@obsessd.ai">hello@obsessd.ai</a></p>
          </section>

          <section>
            <h2>Build a Business AI Can't Commoditise: What Buyers Will Value in Three Years</h2>
            <p>If AI can make almost anything faster, cheaper and easier to replicate, what stops your business becoming a commodity?</p>
            <p>At humAIn, Julia Vargiu, Director Australia at SI Global, challenged workshop participants to look at their businesses through the eyes of a potential acquirer.</p>
            <p>As M&amp;A advisers working with entrepreneurs and founders of marketing, digital and technology businesses, SI Global understands what makes a company attractive to buyers and how AI is changing what they'll value in the years ahead.</p>
            <p>Julia introduced six lenses to help participants examine how AI could affect the value of their business through the eyes of a potential acquirer, identifying where AI might strengthen their competitive advantage, erode existing value or create new opportunities for growth.</p>
            <p>Missed the workshop? Julia is offering delegates a PDF of her presentation and the Buyer Future Fit Map, plus a complimentary 30-minute consultation to discuss their findings and explore opportunities to strengthen the future value of their business.</p>
            <p>To request the materials or arrange a consultation, email Julia at <a href="mailto:julia.vargiu@siglobal.com">julia.vargiu@siglobal.com</a>.</p>
          </section>

        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .res-page { padding: 48px 0 100px; }
  .res-body { max-width: 740px; }
  .res-body p {
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: #fff;
    margin: 0 0 18px;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }
  .res-body h2 {
    font-family: var(--disp);
    font-weight: 800;
    font-size: clamp(24px, 3.4vw, 34px);
    line-height: 1.15;
    letter-spacing: -.02em;
    margin: 16px 0 16px;
    padding-top: 20px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line-2);
  }
  .res-body .res-thanks {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 12px;
    letter-spacing: .08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--pink);
    margin: 16px 0 0;
  }
  .res-thanks + h2 { margin-top: 12px; border-top: 0; padding-top: 0; }
  .res-fig { margin: 0 0 20px; }
  .res-fig img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    border-radius: 6px;
  }
  /* Square and portrait photos would tower over the text at full column width. */
  .res-fig--sq img { max-width: 480px; }
  .res-fig--tall img { max-width: 360px; }
  .res-body a { color: var(--pink); text-decoration: underline; }
</style>
